{
  "$comment": "Spring AI (`org.springframework.ai`, Java and Kotlin). The code talks to beans the starter of the build configures: a `ChatClient` (from an injected `ChatClient.Builder`, or `ChatClient.create(model)` / `ChatClient.builder(model)...build()`) whose fluent chain `prompt(...).user(...).options(...).call()` is one request, sent at `call()` or `stream()`; a `ChatModel` (`call(prompt)`, `stream(prompt)`), an `EmbeddingModel` (`embed`, `call`), an `ImageModel`, a transcription or speech model. The interfaces are shared by every provider: the provider is the one model starter (or module) the manifests declare, else the provider of the model class the `ChatClient` is built on, else unknown (no call). A provider's own classes (`OpenAiChatModel`) are that provider's. The model is the one the code's options set (`OpenAiChatOptions.builder().model(m)`, in `options(...)` or the request object's second argument), else the `spring.ai.<provider>.*.model` property of `application.yml` / `application.properties`; the base URL the `base-url` property (or the `baseUrl(...)` of an API object the code builds). One entry per provider, artifact and model kind (`src/lang/jvm/registry/spring-ai.ts`).",
